# Apps Gateway paths & navigation

When editing routes or SPA routers:

1. Load `authn-implementations/data/paths.json`
2. Do **not** register `/auth/**` or `/actuator/**` as app routes
3. Put the app's **own** anonymous endpoints under `/dangerously-skip-login/**` only
4. The four **gateway probe paths** — exact `/health`, `/api/health`, `/version`, `/api/version` — are
   the exception: implement them at the root, unauthenticated, reading no identity. The gateway routes
   them directly to the app by design, so they are never a path violation. Non-default probe paths go
   in `.platform/observability.yaml`.
5. Use `window.location.assign` (or plain `<a href>`) for `/auth/ui/login` and `/auth/logout` — never `router.push` / framework `<Link>` for those paths
6. Prefer `/dev-login` for local mock login (see skill `local-authn-dev`)
